 MakeTestWB (filename password protect);xl;wb;ws;r;c;fmt;data
 ⍝ Create an Excel test workbook with hidden rows and columns via COM.
 ⍝ filename: path to save; extension determines format (.xlsx or .xls)
 ⍝ password (optional left arg): open password to protect the workbook

 ⍝ Determine Excel file format from extension
 ⍝ xlOpenXMLWorkbook (.xlsx) / xlWorkbookNormal (.xls)
 fmt←(51 ¯4143 0)['.xlsx' '.xls' ⍳ ⎕C 3⌷⎕NPARTS filename]
 'Filename extension must be .xls or .xlsx' ⎕SIGNAL (fmt=0)/11

 'xl' ⎕WC 'OLEClient' 'Excel.Application'
 xl.(Visible DisplayAlerts)←0

 wb←xl.Workbooks.Add ⍬
 ws←wb.ActiveSheet
 ws.Name←'TestData'

 ⍝ Fill 20×10 grid with labelled values
 data←{'R',(⍕⍵[1]),' C',(⍕⍵[2])}¨⍳20 10
 ws.Range[⊂'A1:J20'].Value2←data

 ⍝ ws.(Rows[3 7 12],Columns[2 5]).Hidden←1 ⍝ Hide some rows and columns
⍝ wb.Protect protect 1 1 ⍝ Password, Structure and Windows
 wb.SaveAs filename fmt,(0≠≢password)/⊂password

 wb.Close 0
 xl.Quit
